{
  "_comment": [
    "Deterministic failure seeds for Plan B \u00a712.4, scenario B21.",
    "Each seed names one defect the internal/conformance/shim implementation can be built with,",
    "the semantic category \u00a712.1 places it in, and the exact requirements the suite must fail",
    "when judging that implementation. A seed whose must_fail list stops being failed means the",
    "suite has stopped asserting something it used to assert, which is the regression this file",
    "exists to catch. must_not_fail names rows that must keep passing, so a defect cannot be",
    "'caught' by a suite that simply fails everything.",
    "The seeds are sanitized: the shim holds no credential and the canary secret in it is",
    "synthetic and exists only inside a test process."
